course: dictionary
lesson: 8476
title: A good Samaritan
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A Samaritan was a person from Samaria, a region in the Bible. Today, a good Samaritan is someone who helps a stranger in trouble. The word can be a noun (a good Samaritan) or an adjective (Samaritan).
explain: In Jesus' story, «a Samaritan stopped, bandaged him and paid for his care» after a priest and a Levite walked past the injured traveller. The clues are in the actions: the others passed by, but the Samaritan stopped to help. Ask yourself what he did that the others did not.
explain: Samaritan can also name a charity in the UK. The Samaritans, with a capital S and no "a", is the name of the helpline, so it means the charity, not a person from Samaria. Look for the capital letter and the context to tell which meaning is meant.
fact: A Samaritan was a person from Samaria.
fact: A good Samaritan is anyone who helps a stranger in trouble.
fact: In Jesus' parable, a Samaritan helped a beaten traveller when others walked past.
fact: Jews and Samaritans in Jesus' time usually kept apart.
fact: The Samaritans is a charity you can phone any time to talk if you feel very sad or alone.
exercise: In the story, what did the Samaritan do when others walked past? | Asked for money first | *Stopped, bandaged the man and paid for his care | Walked on by too | Ran away fast
exercise: A news story says «a good Samaritan pulled the driver from the car after the crash». What is a good Samaritan? | A police officer on duty | A driver who is always late | A person from the Samaria region of the Bible | *A stranger who helps someone in trouble
exercise: Find and copy the word that names the group of people Jesus' listeners disliked. | parable | neighbour | command | *Samaritan
test: Which phrase best matches a good Samaritan? | A runner who wins every race | A quiet teacher who never speaks | A person who walks past someone in trouble | *Someone who helps a stranger in trouble
test: Which sentence uses Samaritan as the name of the charity? | Jesus told a story about a traveller | Jews and Samaritans usually kept apart | A Samaritan woman met Jesus at a well | *You can phone the Samaritans any time if you feel very alone
exam: Ella reads «call the Samaritans» and thinks it means ring a person from Samaria. What does it mean? | Ask a stranger for directions | Send a letter to a priest | Visit a town called Samaria | *Phone a charity you can talk to any time when you feel very sad or alone
